WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — three-body (45s) Narrator Bill

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:07.456
First, most big computer failures happen at the handoffs between teams or parts, not inside them.

2
00:00:07.896 --> 00:00:14.587
Second, the cause is usually a guess nobody wrote down, like which units a number uses.

3
00:00:15.027 --> 00:00:20.080
Third, when every handoff guess is written down and machine-checked,

4
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.383
a fix in one place stays fixed.

5
00:00:22.823 --> 00:00:32.012
Space engineers lost the Mars Climate Orbiter because one team sent thruster data in pounds while another read metric newtons.

6
00:00:32.012 --> 00:00:39.815
Like three orbiting stars, theorists, builders, and users drift chaotically whenever handoffs go unchecked.

7
00:00:40.255 --> 00:00:45.308
Because autonomous AI agents cannot rely on unspoken office folklore,

8
00:00:45.308 --> 00:00:52.119
making software safe for AI forces every boundary assumption into a machine-checked contract.
